WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:02.724
Grid Bot Builder. Grid Bot Blueprint.

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:05.683
Lesson two. What you are going to need.

00:00:06.742 --> 00:00:10.465
Education only. Not financial advice. This

00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:12.744
is general information and doesn't

00:00:12.744 --> 00:00:15.100
consider your objectives, financial

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.094
situation or needs. Crypto is high risk.

00:00:18.554 --> 00:00:20.778
You could lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.469 --> 00:00:26.775
Crypto carries a risk of total loss. The

00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:29.418
prices are public historical daily closes,

00:00:29.418 --> 00:00:34.838
marked Example. Past performance is not a

00:00:34.838 --> 00:00:40.150
reliable indicator of future results. A

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.374
packing list is written before the trip,

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.708
not during the scramble at the door. The

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:47.177
list is the analogy, and the chart is the

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:49.965
public prices we already have. You need

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:51.854
the page before you need a screen.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:53.915
Beginners go wrong when they open a

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.795
trading screen before their plan is

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:58.836
written down. You need a page before you

00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:01.411
need a screen. People lose the lesson when

00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:03.524
they open a form while the notebook is

00:01:03.337 --> 00:01:08.934
still blank. By the end you will fill in a

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.851
seven-item checklist from the July to

00:01:11.851 --> 00:01:17.544
October 2023 example, on paper. You will

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:22.645
keep every secret off that page. You will

00:01:22.645 --> 00:01:24.900
mark the page Example so nobody can read

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.070
it as an order. The seven items are: a

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.052
notebook, the three words range levels and

00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:35.608
stop, the pair, paper or a demo account,

00:01:35.608 --> 00:01:38.249
no secrets, a written stop, and the word

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:41.199
Example on every figure. A pair is what

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:43.783
you buy and what you pay with. For this

00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:45.972
course the pair is bitcoin priced in US

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.712
dollars. A demo account uses pretend

00:01:48.712 --> 00:01:51.479
money. A daily close is the last price of

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:53.754
the day. You are naming that public

00:01:53.754 --> 00:01:56.913
series, not choosing an app. Carry the

00:01:56.913 --> 00:01:59.722
three words forward from the July to

00:01:59.722 --> 00:02:03.271
October 2023 example in lesson 1. Range:

00:02:03.527 --> 00:02:10.388
24930 to 30331. Levels: six gaps of about

00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:14.046
900. Stop: a rule you write before you

00:02:14.046 --> 00:02:17.842
start, for when the close leaves 30331 and

00:02:17.842 --> 00:02:20.745
does not come back, as it did on 23

00:02:20.745 --> 00:02:23.815
October 2023. If you can only say one of

00:02:23.815 --> 00:02:25.928
the three words, the page is missing a

00:02:25.887 --> 00:02:29.025
part. The three words are range, levels,

00:02:29.025 --> 00:02:30.935
and stop, carried forward from the

00:02:30.935 --> 00:02:33.794
introduction. The checklist asks for them

00:02:33.794 --> 00:02:35.857
so a later form has something true to

00:02:35.857 --> 00:02:40.337
copy. You never type a seed phrase, a

00:02:40.337 --> 00:02:42.964
private key, or an A P I secret onto this

00:02:42.964 --> 00:02:46.090
page. The chart has no balance on it. A

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.625
public close is not your account. If a

00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:51.033
form asks for a secret, that form is not

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:54.867
this lesson. You never type a seed phrase,

00:02:54.867 --> 00:02:57.438
a private key, or an API secret into a

00:02:57.438 --> 00:03:00.222
lesson, a chat, or a form. The course can

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:02.642
teach the shape of a field. It cannot be

00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:04.755
trusted with a secret, and it will not

00:03:04.695 --> 00:03:09.965
ask. You copy the band onto the page, not

00:03:09.965 --> 00:03:14.306
every day's prices. The low was 24930 and

00:03:14.306 --> 00:03:19.517
the high was 30331, with six gaps of about

00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:22.298
900. Every close in that window stayed

00:03:22.298 --> 00:03:25.075
inside the band. Mark each figure Example.

00:03:26.095 --> 00:03:28.526
Worked check: pair, band, gaps, stop, and

00:03:28.526 --> 00:03:31.324
Example. If the stop line is only a tick

00:03:31.324 --> 00:03:33.465
with no sentence, the page fails the

00:03:33.465 --> 00:03:36.857
check. The rule has to say: if the daily

00:03:36.857 --> 00:03:40.241
close goes above 30331 and does not come

00:03:40.241 --> 00:03:44.003
back, the example is over. Say the page

00:03:44.003 --> 00:03:46.348
once, in your own words. The pair is

00:03:46.348 --> 00:03:48.483
bitcoin, and a daily close is the last

00:03:48.483 --> 00:03:52.779
price of the day. The band is 24930 to

00:03:52.779 --> 00:03:58.249
30331, with six gaps of about 900. The

00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:01.060
stop rule says what you will do if the

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.246
close leaves 30331 and does not come back.

00:04:04.706 --> 00:04:07.542
A secret is a seed phrase, a private key,

00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:10.354
or an API secret. A seed phrase is the

00:04:10.354 --> 00:04:12.460
list of words that unlocks a crypto

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.450
wallet. A private key or an API secret is

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.517
a password that can move your money. None

00:04:18.517 --> 00:04:21.082
of those go on this page. Example on a

00:04:21.082 --> 00:04:23.462
figure means a real past price, not a

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:26.859
forecast, and not an order. The setup

00:04:26.859 --> 00:04:29.637
check has seven items: notebook, the three

00:04:29.637 --> 00:04:31.761
words, pair name, paper or demo, no

00:04:31.761 --> 00:04:34.131
secrets, a written stop, and the word

00:04:34.131 --> 00:04:37.183
Example. Each line is a fact. A tick

00:04:37.183 --> 00:04:40.374
without the fact is decoration. A pair

00:04:40.374 --> 00:04:42.610
name is two assets written with a slash,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.723
the coin you buy and the money you pay

00:04:44.705 --> 00:04:47.292
with. An empty pair slot is a missing

00:04:47.292 --> 00:04:50.131
fact. It is not a detail you will remember

00:04:50.131 --> 00:04:55.354
later. The screen, when you reach it, is

00:04:55.354 --> 00:04:57.817
paper or demo. Paper lets you see the

00:04:57.817 --> 00:05:00.194
fields. It does not send an order, and

00:05:00.194 --> 00:05:02.361
this course never asks you to send one.

00:05:05.224 --> 00:05:07.289
The stop line on the checklist is a

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:09.892
sentence, not a tick. The sentence says

00:05:09.892 --> 00:05:12.475
what path finishes the idea. A tick with

00:05:12.475 --> 00:05:17.294
no sentence is the common miss. Every

00:05:17.294 --> 00:05:19.681
number and every pair on the page carries

00:05:19.681 --> 00:05:22.307
the word Example. That word is what keeps

00:05:22.307 --> 00:05:24.420
a teaching sketch from being read as a

00:05:24.239 --> 00:05:29.232
recommendation. A profit target is not on

00:05:29.232 --> 00:05:31.973
the list. A leverage multiple is not on

00:05:31.973 --> 00:05:34.696
the list. Those lines would change the

00:05:34.696 --> 00:05:37.028
subject from setup to a result, and this

00:05:37.028 --> 00:05:41.848
lesson has no result. A later button, on

00:05:41.848 --> 00:05:44.749
paper, is only a copy of the page. If the

00:05:44.749 --> 00:05:47.072
page is blank, the form has nothing true

00:05:47.072 --> 00:05:49.323
to copy, and the button does not invent

00:05:49.323 --> 00:05:54.370
it. You are early in the course. The

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.548
definition, the regime, and the spacing

00:05:56.548 --> 00:05:59.131
are still ahead. Finishing the checklist

00:05:59.131 --> 00:06:03.537
does not mean the grid is designed. Look

00:06:03.537 --> 00:06:05.704
at the pair row and imagine it empty on

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.334
purpose. The rest of the list can be tidy

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.668
and the page is still blocked, because the

00:06:10.626 --> 00:06:12.649
form would not know which market the

00:06:12.649 --> 00:06:17.820
drawing belongs to. The common miss is to

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.253
skip the list and open the screen. The

00:06:20.253 --> 00:06:26.608
screen will ask for the same facts, and it
will accept blanks that your page should

00:06:26.608 --> 00:06:29.631
have refused. The action is to complete

00:06:29.631 --> 00:06:32.558
the seven items on paper today. Read each

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.268
answer out loud. If a line has no answer,

00:06:35.268 --> 00:06:40.263
it is not done. The page comes before the

00:06:40.263 --> 00:06:45.061
screen. Recap for What you are going to

00:06:45.061 --> 00:06:47.545
need. Say the hook in one line, name the

00:06:47.545 --> 00:06:49.712
diagram you drew, and name the line you

00:06:49.681 --> 00:06:52.173
wrote in the notebook. If one of those

00:06:52.173 --> 00:06:54.119
three is missing, the lesson is not

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:59.176
finished. The figures are the summer low,

00:06:59.176 --> 00:07:04.159
the summer high, and six gaps. Secrets

00:07:04.159 --> 00:07:06.928
stay off the page. Example stays on it.

00:07:09.898 --> 00:07:12.676
Next lesson: What is a grid bot. Bring

00:07:12.676 --> 00:07:14.732
your notes: the top and bottom of the

00:07:14.623 --> 00:07:16.957
band, the gaps between the lines, and your

00:07:16.839 --> 00:07:19.734
stop rule. Leave every figure marked

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:22.099
Example. No order is sent between lessons.

